{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "To fair Japan, thou dost travel, let me weave a tale in verse, a journey through time and space, as Shakespeare might have penned it.\n\nFirst, thou shalt land in Tokyo, city of lights and life so bright, where neon lights dance in the night, and ancient tradition meets the modern sight. Visit the Meiji Shrine, a sacred place, where nature's grace doth embrace, and the bustling markets of Harajuku, where fashion's bold and free.\n\nNext, thy journey leads to Kyoto, city of a thousand temples, where the scent of incense fills the air, and history whispers in every square. Walk the Philosopher's Path, a journey of the mind, where cherry blossoms bloom in springtime's find.\n\nThen, to Nara, where deer roam free, and temples stand with majesty, in a park so green and wide. Feed the deer with crackers, a gentle deed, and feel the peace that here does proceed.\n\nFrom there, to Osaka, city of laughter and cheer, where food is king and joyous is the year. Try the takoyaki, a delight to eat, and the okonomiyaki, a savory treat.\n\nFurther north, to Hokkaido, land of snow and ice, where nature's majesty does not cease. Visit the Shiretoko, a UNESCO site, where nature's beauty takes the light.\n\nLastly, to Hiroshima, a city of peace, where history teaches a lesson so clear. The Peace Memorial Park, a place of somber thought, where the world is reminded of the cost, and the hope for a peaceful lot.\n\nThus, thy journey in Japan, a tapestry of scenes, where old and new, tradition and dream, blend in a dance that's ever seen. And when thou returnest home, the memories of this land, in thy heart, will forever stand.", "logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -2.5828957557678223}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -1.7366130352020264}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.06187696382403374}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.9554200172424316}, {"token": " thou", "logp